 Because `frai-core` is a regular ESM package, you can import only the modules you need and embed FRAI capabilities inside automation pipelines, CI jobs, or custom products.
 
+Example: run evaluations with threshold gating.
+
+```ts
+import { Eval } from 'frai-core';
+
+const dataset = Eval.loadDataset({
+  outputsPath: './outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: './references.json'
+});
+
+const evaluations = Eval.runEvaluations({
+  outputs: dataset.outputs,
+  references: dataset.references
+});
+
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: dataset.outputsPath,
+  referencesPath: dataset.referencesPath,
+  thresholds: { exact_match: 0.9, toxicity: 0.95 }
+});
+
+// report.passed is true if all thresholds pass
+if (!report.passed) {
+  console.log('Evaluation failed:', report.thresholds);
+  process.exit(1);
+}
+
+const path = Eval.writeReport({ report, format: 'json' });
+console.log('Report written to', path);
+```
+
+The `generateReport` function accepts an optional `thresholds` object (e.g., `{ exact_match: 0.9 }`) and adds `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array with `{ metric, min, score, passed }` entries) to the report. A metric with no score (e.g., exact match without references) fails its threshold. This works with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations` as long as they include an `id` field.
+
